From a01ed569b6e6d29aaf4009e368323f695a3fccb5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 17:40:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ggml-cpu): same g64 stride defect in the ported x86 Q2_0
 vec_dot

SEPARATE from the GEMM fix on purpose. This is a different function, on a
different selection mechanism, found only because it invalidated the control
arm used to verify the GEMM fix.

c7645a0df added a native x86 ggml_vec_dot_q2_0_q8_0 and removed the
arch-fallback alias to the generic one. That commit stated plainly that
PrismML's bit-exactness claim was 'not independently re-verified here beyond
reading that the two branches compute the same expression'. Re-verified now:
FALSIFIED. The two branches do compute the same expression as each other -
both compute the g128 one.

Both the VNNI branch and its scalar #else carry PrismML's g128 literals:
  for (int k = 0; k < 4; k++)  over  &y[i * 4 + k]
On this g64 fork QK2_0/QK8_0 == 2, so the activation pointer runs at twice the
rate the loop consumes, and &x[i].qs[k * 8] reads at offsets 16 and 24 of a
16-byte block_q2_0.qs - out of bounds into the following block. Reads stay
inside the mapped tensor, so the failure is silent wrong numbers rather than
NaN. The generic ggml_vec_dot_q2_0_q8_0_generic (quants.c:203-204) was already
correct (k < 2, y[i * 2 + k]); the x86 arm now matches it.

Why this matters beyond the two lines: ggml_vec_dot_q2_0_q8_0 is selected at
COMPILE time, so it sits outside GGML_ARIFI_VNNI_REPACK. The toggle's
documented promise that '=0 restores the exact pre-slot behaviour on every
architecture' was therefore false on x86 - '=0' selected a different NEW
kernel, not the pre-slot one. Every ON/OFF comparison recorded in this slot
before today compared one broken kernel against a differently broken kernel,
and none of them adjudicated anything.

Measured effect, same rig and flags as the GEMM fix, repack OFF arm,
qwen2.5-0.5b-light-q8_0-4xffndownQ2_0-g64.gguf:
  before: 'ering!!!!!!!!!!!!...'  (garbage, though deterministic)
  after:  token-identical to the repack ON arm, md5 bf102b77..., 32/32 tokens
The unquantized fp16 source model produces the same continuation, so the
repaired path tracks the reference rather than merely agreeing with itself.

NOT claimed: bit-identity. The first-token top-3 logprobs still differ between
the repack and vec_dot arms (-1.5831375122070312 vs -1.4819049835205078). Both
arms are internally deterministic, so that is a real residual divergence and is
recorded as an open finding in the registry, not papered over.

Ported-mechanism: g128 -> g64 stride parameterization (2 lines)
Source-path: ggml/src/ggml-cpu/arch/x86/quants.c
Evidence: research/local-inference/trial-evidence/110/vnni-g64-fix/
Origin: ArifiLabs/vnni-repack
---
 ggml/src/ggml-cpu/arch/x86/quants.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/arch/x86/quants.c b/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/arch/x86/quants.c
index dbe83a6f3..5d927bf66 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/arch/x86/quants.c
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/arch/x86/quants.c
@@ -585,8 +585,8 @@ void ggml_vec_dot_q2_0_q8_0(int n, float * GGML_RESTRICT s, size_t bs, const voi
     for (int i = 0; i < nb; i++) {
         const float d0 = GGML_CPU_FP16_TO_FP32(x[i].d);
         float sumi = 0.0f;
-        for (int k = 0; k < 4; k++) {
-            const block_q8_0 * GGML_RESTRICT yb = &y[i * 4 + k];
+        for (int k = 0; k < QK2_0 / QK8_0; k++) {
+            const block_q8_0 * GGML_RESTRICT yb = &y[i * (QK2_0 / QK8_0) + k];
             const float d1 = GGML_CPU_FP16_TO_FP32(yb->d);
             const __m256i qy = _mm256_loadu_si256((const __m256i *) yb->qs);
             const __m128i src = _mm_loadl_epi64((const __m128i *) &x[i].qs[k * 8]); // 8 bytes
@@ -609,8 +609,8 @@ void ggml_vec_dot_q2_0_q8_0(int n, float * GGML_RESTRICT s, size_t bs, const voi
 
         float sumi = 0.0f;
 
-        for (int k = 0; k < 4; k++) {
-            const block_q8_0 * GGML_RESTRICT yb = &y[i * 4 + k];
+        for (int k = 0; k < QK2_0 / QK8_0; k++) {
+            const block_q8_0 * GGML_RESTRICT yb = &y[i * (QK2_0 / QK8_0) + k];
             const float d1 = GGML_CPU_FP16_TO_FP32(yb->d);
             int sumi_block = 0;
 
